  "notes": "FORMS:\n{手|て} (hand) + {入|い}れる (to put in)\n\nLiterally 'putting in hands' → giving attention to.\n- {手入|てい}れする - to maintain, to care for\n- {手入|てい}れを{行|おこな}う - to perform maintenance (formal)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {庭|にわ}の{手入|てい}れ - garden maintenance\n- {肌|はだ}/{髪|かみ}の{手入|てい}れ - skincare/haircare\n- {道具|どうぐ}の{手入|てい}れ - tool maintenance\n- {手入|てい}れが{行|い}き{届|とど}いている - well-maintained\n- {警察|けいさつ}の{手入|てい}れ - police raid\n\nSECOND MEANING:\nThe sense of 'raid' comes from the idea of police 'putting their hands into' an establishment.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- メンテナンス - maintenance (loanword)\n- {整備|せいび} - maintenance (machines, systems)\n- {世話|せわ} - care, looking after",
